{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794269552,"nonce":"+0TlKOhKXiO02caKi/j8odFrqyQ=","title":"Key to picture on desktop is the wait for the next 60 Hz frame plus 2 to 4 ms; typing never rebuilds","message":"Live probe (fs-tasks title field, 8 keys through fake_input, nested KWin). Key press to end of the frame that shows it: 3.9, 4.1, 9.0, 10.8, 13.3, 13.8, 14.8, 18.8 ms (min 3.9, max 18.8). The frame itself costs 2.2 to 4.2 ms (p1 about 1 ms of which is the state-style check, p4 0.8 to 1.6 ms); the event handler costs 0.1 to 0.4 ms. No rebuild happens while typing; the difference between the keys is where in the 16.7 ms frame cadence the key arrives. So the floor for typing is half a frame on average, set by the cadence; p1 (about 1 ms) appears on frames with input and could be looked at.\nThis does not include the compositor's own latency to the screen (not measurable in nested KWin).","files":null}]}